  "body": "Faster TUI startup on large scans:\n\n- Duplicate-group total sizes were previously recomputed via `os.Stat()` on every file when building the TUI view model, even though the size was already known from the scan. On scans of ~2M files this meant hundreds of thousands of blocking, single-threaded `stat()` syscalls before the TUI could render its first frame.\n- File sizes are now cached at scan time and reused when building duplicate-group summaries, falling back to a stat only when a size wasn't already known (currently just fuzzy-match groups).\n\nNo CLI/flag changes since v0.6.2."
